From 0015802f7acc55ed3dd5dd432af4ac2d8993170b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:56:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(frames): a child frame lays out with its own stylesheets
 and images

A frame realm resolved layout against its own document but nothing fetched
that document's resources: its <link rel=stylesheet> never applied and its
images never loaded (frame renderer caches cannot load synchronously, and
no one serviced their misses). A frame's box styled by its own sheet read
388x18 instead of 123x45, and its 37x21 image read 0x0.

The page's stylesheet fetch and resource scan now take the document they
work for. A frame's stylesheets are fetched and installed before its
scripts run, its images and fonts start loading at attach, its load event
waits for them within the page's warmup budget, and later misses are
serviced with the page's. Frame loads share the page's concurrency limit
and report Network events like the page's.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
